## 1. Executive Summary

ClusterMind is a **production-grade, multi-cluster AI-powered Kubernetes troubleshooting agent** built by Vedant Singh. It consists of a **FastAPI (Python) backend** that connects to live Kubernetes clusters via the official Python client, collects multi-layered diagnostic telemetry (pod status, container logs, K8s events, deployment replica states, network/endpoint health), sends that aggregated evidence to **Groq's LPU-hosted Llama 3.3 70B** model for SRE-level root cause analysis, and returns actionable diagnosis through a **Next.js 14 (App Router) + Tailwind CSS** dark-themed frontend.

The system implements **JWT authentication with bcrypt hashing**, **RBAC-enforced multi-tenancy** (viewer/operator roles per cluster), **human-in-the-loop remediation execution** with an immutable audit trail, **SHA256 evidence TTL caching** to shield Groq rate limits, and **model fallback** from Llama 3.3 70B to Llama 3.1 8B. It is containerized with **multi-stage Docker builds**, orchestrated via **Docker Compose**, and has CI/CD pipelines via **GitHub Actions** targeting **Azure Container Apps** (backend) and **Vercel** (frontend). Secrets are managed through **Azure Key Vault**.

**Implementation status:** All 6 agile increments described in the README are implemented in code. The codebase is functional and complete. The current deployment targets Azure, not AWS — the AWS architecture in this guide is a **proposed alternative deployment**.

