### 6.1 Authentication Flow
```
User (browser)
→ POST /api/v1/auth/login {email, password}
→ FastAPI auth.py router
→ SQLAlchemy query: SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ?
→ passlib bcrypt verify(plain_password, stored_hash)
→ jose.jwt.encode({sub: user_id, exp: 24h})
→ Response: {access_token: "eyJ...", token_type: "bearer"}
→ Frontend stores token in localStorage
```

### 6.2 Investigation Flow (Core)
```
User clicks "Run Diagnostics"
→ Frontend: POST /api/v1/investigations {cluster_id, namespace}
  (Authorization: Bearer <JWT>)
→ FastAPI investigations.py:
  → deps.get_current_user() — JWT validation
  → rate_limiter.check_rate_limit() — 20/hour enforcement
  → deps.verify_cluster_access() — viewer role check
  → SQLAlchemy: INSERT INTO investigations (status="running")
  → keyvault_manager.get_secret(cluster.kubeconfig_secret_ref)
    → Azure Key Vault OR environment variable fallback
  → K8sClientManager.get_api_clients(raw_kubeconfig)
    → tempfile write → load_kube_config() → cleanup → CoreV1Api + AppsV1Api
    → OR: in-cluster config → OR: default kubeconfig → OR: None (synthetic mode)
  → aggregate_cluster_evidence(v1_api, apps_api, namespace):
    → inspect_pods() — list_namespaced_pod → structured data (or synthetic)
    → collect_logs() — read_namespaced_pod_log (current + previous fallback)
    → analyze_events() — list_namespaced_event → filter Warning/Error
    → inspect_deployments() — list_namespaced_deployment → replica states
    → inspect_network() — list_namespaced_service + read_namespaced_endpoints
    → Compute summary flags → Return unified evidence dict
  → analyze_evidence_with_groq(evidence):
    → SHA256 cache check → if hit, return cached
    → Build SRE system prompt + user prompt with evidence JSON
    → httpx.AsyncClient → POST https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/chat/completions
      → model: llama-3.3-70b-versatile, temperature: 0.2, json_object format
      → ON FAILURE: retry with llama-3.1-8b-instant
      → ON DOUBLE FAILURE: return _fallback_response (raw telemetry)
    → Parse JSON: root_cause, suggested_fix, suggested_command, confidence_score
    → Cache result (5-min TTL)
  → UPDATE investigations SET root_cause=?, suggested_fix=?, status="completed"
  → SELECT investigation WITH progress_steps (eager load)
→ Response: InvestigationOut JSON
→ Frontend: Display root cause card, confidence ring, suggested command, evidence tabs
```

